                                    "<div class='cq-part mb-4'><p class='font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200'>(b) How does crop rotation maintain soil fertility? Explain.</p><div class='mt-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300'>Crop rotation is a systematic approach to planting different types of crops in a specific order on the same piece of land. It maintains soil fertility by ensuring that the same nutrients are not exhausted repeatedly by the same type of crop year after year.<br><br><br>By including leguminous crops (like pulses) in the rotation, nitrogen is naturally fixed in the soil through root nodules. Furthermore, different crops have different rooting depths, which prevents the depletion of nutrients from a single soil layer and breaks the life cycle of pests and diseases, keeping the soil healthy and productive.</div></div>"
