                                    "<div class='cq-part mb-4'><p class='font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200'>(c) What type of soil is indicated by 'C' in the stem? Explain.</p><div class='mt-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300'>The soil marked 'C' in the stem is Alkaline Soil (Khariyo Matit). This is because it is positioned on the pH scale in the range greater than 7.0, specifically extending toward 14.<br><br><br>Alkaline soil is characterized by a high concentration of basic cations like Calcium, Magnesium, and Sodium. In Bangladesh, such soils are often found in coastal regions where salt accumulation is high. These soils typically have poor physical structure and low availability of essential micronutrients like Iron, Manganese, and Boron.<br><br><br>Crops grown in 'C' type soil often suffer from nutrient deficiencies. To manage this soil for agriculture, farmers often need to apply gypsum or organic matter to lower the pH and improve the soil's chemical balance, making it more suitable for cultivation.</div></div>",
