                                    "<div class='cq-part mb-4'><p class='font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200'>(d) Between Image-A and Image-B shown in the stem, which one will be more effective in the agricultural sector of Bangladesh? Give arguments in favor of your opinion.</p><div class='mt-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300'>In the context of \"Digital Bangladesh\" and the current modernization of the sector, Image-B (e-Agriculture/ICT use) will be more effective in the long run, although both methods have their specific roles.<br><br><br>Speed and Wide Reach: While a physical meeting (Image-A) is limited by time, location, and the number of participants, e-Agriculture (Image-B) can reach millions of farmers instantly. Using laptops or smartphones, farmers can access a global database of information, weather forecasts, and market prices from anywhere at any time.<br><br><br>Precision and Visual Learning: Digital platforms allow farmers to watch high-quality tutorials and use diagnostic apps for pest and disease identification. This provides a level of technical precision that a verbal discussion in a group meeting might lack, helping farmers apply modern scientific solutions accurately in their fields.<br><br><br>Overcoming Logistics and Labor Shortages: As the rural workforce shifts, the ability for a single farmer to use technology to manage large areas or get expert help without waiting for a physical visit from an officer is a game-changer. Digital services like the \"Krishi Batayon\" or call centers provide 24/7 support, which is crucial during emergencies like sudden pest outbreaks or natural disasters.<br><br><br>Conclusion: While group meetings are excellent for social mobilization and building initial trust, the scalability, accuracy, and real-time nature of ICT-based agriculture (Image-B) make it the most powerful tool for transforming Bangladesh into a high-tech, profitable agricultural nation. Investing in digital literacy for farmers is the most effective path toward sustainable food security.</div></div>"
